vity to cetuximab treatment was tested. This model showed high sensitivity to this drug. We induced acquired resistance to anti-EGFR therapy in this sensitive model by treating it chronically with anti-EGFR monoclonal antibody (cetuximab, 30 mg/kg/week) until resistance ensues. RNA-seq analysis was performed on samples coming from untreated and cetuximab-resistant PDX, revealing major changes of expression at the mRNA level.","gpl":"24676","gse":"307896","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/06/22","suppfile":"XLS","samples":[{"accession":"GSM9233674","title":"resistant to cetuximab HNC004 biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9233677","title":"resistant to cetuximab HNC004 biol rep6"},{"accession":"GSM9233672","title":"resistant to cetuximab HNC004 biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9233675","title":"resistant to cetuximab HNC004 biol rep4"},{"accession":"GSM9233679","title":"baseline HNC004 biol rep2"},{"accession":"GSM9233678","title":"baseline HNC004 biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9233676","title":"resistant to cetuximab HNC004 biol rep5"},{"accession":"GSM9233673","title":"resistant to cetuximab HNC004 biol rep2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":8,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE307nnn/GSE307896/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1327762"},"200306480":{"uid":"200306480","accession":"GSE306480","gds":"","title":"Analysis of cetuximab-induced gene expression changes in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma cell lines","summary":"Despite recent advances in immunotherapy and anti-epidermal growth factor receptor (EGFR) treatments, the therapeutic landscape for locally advanced HNSCC has changed little over recent decades, and clinical outcome remains poor. Cetuximab, monoclonal antibody targeting EGFR, offers only modest and often transient clinical responses, owing to the persistence of a therapy-tolerant cell population that seeds residual disease and eventual therapeutic failure. Clinical evidence across cancer types indicates that depth of response to targeted therapy correlates with prolonged progression-free survival, highlighting the importance of residual disease as a driver of resistance. However, the molecular features enabling HNSCC cells to tolerate EGFR blockade before the acquisition of stable resistance remain incompletely understood. To uncover early transcriptional adaptations to EGFR inhibition, we performed bulk RNA-sequencing on FaDu and HN5 HNSCC cells treated with cetuximab for 72 hours.","gpl":"30173","gse":"306480","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/06/22","suppfile":"XLS","samples":[{"accession":"GSM9201931","title":"Vehicle-treated FaDu cells_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9201934","title":"Cetuximab-treated FaDu cells_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9201940","title":"Cetuximab-treated HN5 cells_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9201937","title":"Vehicle-treated HN5 cells_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9201929","title":"Vehicle-treated FaDu cells_biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9201936","title":"Vehicle-treated HN5 cells_biol rep2"},{"accession":"GSM9201932","title":"Cetuximab-treated FaDu cells_biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9201939","title":"Cetuximab-treated HN5 cells_biol rep2"},{"accession":"GSM9201933","title":"Cetuximab-treated FaDu cells_biol rep2"},{"accession":"GSM9201935","title":"Vehicle-treated HN5 cells_biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9201938","title":"Cetuximab-treated HN5 cells_biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9201930","title":"Vehicle-treated FaDu cells_biol rep2"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":12,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":[],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE306nnn/GSE306480/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1310947"},"200303798":{"uid":"200303798","accession":"GSE303798","gds":"","title":"Evaluation of cetuximab-induced gene expression changes in residual PDX tumors of head and neck squamous cell carcinoma","summary":"Cetuximab, a monoclonal antibody targeting EGFR, offers only modest and often transient clinical responses in recurrent or metastatic HNSCC, owing to the persistence of a therapy-tolerant cell population that seeds residual disease and eventual therapeutic failure. Clinical evidence across cancer types indicates that depth of response to targeted therapy correlates with prolonged progression-free survival, highlighting the importance of residual disease as a driver of resistance. However, the molecular features enabling HNSCC cells to tolerate EGFR blockade before the acquisition of stable resistance remain incompletely understood. We analyzed residual tumors from cetuximab-treated patient-derived xenograft (PDX) models of HNSCC (#UCLHN04 and #HNC004) to identify gene expression changes associated with anti-EGFR tolerance in HNSCC cells.","gpl":"24676","gse":"303798","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/06/22","suppfile":"XLSX","samples":[{"accession":"GSM9136156","title":"Vehicle-treated residual HNC004 PDX_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9136153","title":"Vehicle-treated residual HNC004 PDX_biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9136162","title":"Cetuximab-treated residual UCLHN04 PDX_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9136159","title":"Cetuximab-treated residual UCLHN04 PDX_biol rep1"},{"accession":"GSM9136163","title":"Vehicle-treated residual UCLHN04 PDX_biol rep3"},{"accession":"GSM9136160","title":"Cetuximab-treated residual UCLHN04 PDX_biol rep2"},{"accession":"GSM9136157","title":"Cetuximab-treated residual HNC004 PDX_biol rep3"},{"accession":"