 (TGFβ) in trNK cell differentiation has been demonstrated, the context in which the differentiation of CD49a+CD103+ trNK cells occurs can result in either an immunosuppressive phenotype or a highly cytotoxic one. To understand this dichotomy better, we utilized a multiomics approach to molecularly characterize these cells and identified a highly cytotoxic trNK (ctrNK) cell phenotype, characterized by the expression of CD39.","gpl":"24676","gse":"284447","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing; Other","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/05/04","suppfile":"CSV","samples":[{"accession":"GSM8684452","title":"CITEseq:ieILC1 ADT"},{"accession":"GSM8684451","title":"CITEseq:ieILC1 GEX"},{"accession":"GSM8684453","title":"CITEseq:ieILC1 HTO"}],"relations":[],"extrelations":[],"n_samples":3,"seriestitle":"","platformtitle":"","platformtaxa":"","samplestaxa":"","pubmedids":["42090477"],"projects":[],"ftplink":"ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/series/GSE284nnn/GSE284447/","geo2r":"no","bioproject":"PRJNA1199027"},"200314413":{"uid":"200314413","accession":"GSE314413","gds":"","title":"High throughput sequencing of T cells from a patient undergoing immune checkpoint inhibitor therapy [P365-5]","summary":"This is part of a prospective longitudinal study designed to identify biomarkers predictive of the onset of irAEs associated with ICI therapy and determine whether these biomarkers are further related to treatment efficacy. This experiment was a pilot study of CD8 T-cells from three visits of a single donor.","gpl":"30173","gse":"314413","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2026/05/01","suppfile":"CSV, H5","samples":[{"accession":"GSM9395998","title":"GEX visit 1"},{"accession":"GSM9396004","title":"FB visit 1"},{"accession":"GSM9396001","title":"TCR visit